#!/bin/bash
# codesage-prompt-override
#
# Print a system-prompt fragment that steers Claude Code to prefer
# CodeSage's MCP tools over Grep for retrieval-shape tasks. Pipe into
# `claude --append-system-prompt-file -` or paste into a `~/.claude/
# settings.json` `appendSystemPrompt` slot.
#
# Pattern adopted from Serena's `cc-system-prompt-override` (see
# notes/20260429-reference-tool-recommendations.md §1.7 / §2.3
# rerun 2026-04-30: prompt-level hardening of tool descriptions did
# not move tool-selection rate from 0%, so the system-prompt slot is
# the next lever).

cat <<'EOF'

# CodeSage MCP tool selection

When the active project has a `.codesage/index.db` directory, the
`mcp__codesage__*` tools answer retrieval and code-graph questions
faster and more precisely than `Grep`. Pick the right tool by the
shape of the question:

| Question shape | Tool |
|---|---|
| "What is this codebase?" / starting work / "where do I begin?" (one bounded orientation: languages, freshness, features, top risk, conventions, next calls) | `mcp__codesage__project_overview` |
| "Where is <Identifier> defined?" (function, class, struct, enum, constant, macro) | `mcp__codesage__find_symbol` |
| "Where is <Identifier> called / imported / inherited from / instantiated?" | `mcp__codesage__find_references` |
| "Where does <concept> happen?" / "Where is auth, config, retries, logging handled?" / paraphrase queries | `mcp__codesage__search` |
| "What does `path/file.rs` import, and who imports it?" | `mcp__codesage__list_dependencies` |
| "What files break if I rename / change <Symbol>?" | `mcp__codesage__impact_analysis` |
| "Bundle code for this concept for another LLM." | `mcp__codesage__export_context` |
| "What's the risk of this patch?" / "What tests should I run?" / "What files co-change with this one?" | `mcp__codesage__assess_risk` / `mcp__codesage__assess_risk_diff` / `mcp__codesage__recommend_tests` / `mcp__codesage__find_coupling` |
| "Before I commit — what will a reviewer flag?" (missing tests, risky/blast-radius files, cycles, trust boundaries, feature-test gaps, scope creep) | `mcp__codesage__review_rehearsal` |

Use `Grep` / `Glob` / `Bash` only when the target is a non-identifier
literal: error messages, log text, config keys, TODO/FIXME markers,
quoted strings, cross-cutting English ("deprecated", "FIXME"). If the
pattern matches `[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*` or is a `|`-joined list of
such tokens, the question is symbol-shaped and the CodeSage tools win
in one call where Grep would take 3-5.

CodeSage tools all require an absolute `project` argument. Read it
from the project's `.claude/CLAUDE.md` (the codesage onboarder writes
the path there) or use the current working directory's absolute form.

If a CodeSage tool returns an empty or "not onboarded" result for a
project, fall back to Grep — but state which tool you tried first and
why it didn't fit, so the user can spot a missing index.
EOF
